<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>This isn't really an SCP article at all, but a tale with a proposal for one (that doesn't even exist).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Though I'm certainly not a fan, I think there's enough precedence to consider this as a mainlist entry. *cough cough* <a href="/scp-2864">SCP-2864</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<blockquote>
<p>This is a unique and interesting way of going about an SCP article</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Unique? Not really. I could probably find half a dozen that incorporate interdepartmental memos into the format. This isn't exactly that wild, or much of a stretch.</p>
<p>Interesting? That's debatable. It came off as contrived (in the sense that this information was so readily attainable) and quite frankly, I was bored to death by the lack of anything resembling a compelling narrative.</p>
<p>More deets:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>It's answering a question that, sure, plenty have asked over the years, but not in a way that</p>
<ul>
<li>A) gives me the slightest reason to care about any of the characters (whole plot is kicked off on a lark, and set into motion with just as much naïveté and isn't really resolved in any manner which suggests there was anything lost or gained)</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>B) gives me anything to chew on regarding the wider scope or implications of the story (or lack thereof). Even if it's about the SCPF peddling drugs, hell, I could buy that, but that angle doesn't even seem to be present in the article, so I'm left with generic vagueness and nothing to consider.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
If someone were to ask me &quot;hey, remember that one SCP where they might maybe be hinting at selling drugs except nothing happens and everyone goes home?&quot; I'd answer 'no'.
<p>If you think this is to be lauded as unique and interesting then you're really missing out. Sorry about that.</p>

							</div>

								
					
